# Files that another program executes must keep LF endings. With core.autocrlf=true a
# checkout rewrites them to CRLF, and a `#!/bin/sh` script with CRLF fails as
# `bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M` — the git hook below would then silently stop guarding.
# Git warns about the conversion at `git add` time; that warning is the advance notice
# of exactly how this defence dies.
.githooks/*  text eol=lf
*.sh         text eol=lf
